course: dictionary
lesson: 14300
title: Noxious: harmful or very unpleasant
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Noxious means harmful or poisonous, or very unpleasant. You will often meet it when people talk about gases, fumes and chemicals, because those can hurt your body.
explain: «The smoke from the factory chimney was noxious, so the workers wore masks.» The masks are a clue. People only wear masks to protect themselves from something harmful in the air, so noxious must mean harmful or poisonous. Check it: swap in harmful, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «The bin gave off a noxious smell that made Sam hold his nose.» Here noxious does not mean poisonous. It means very unpleasant. Holding your nose is the clue. Context tells you which meaning the author wants.
explain: In Australia, Canada and the US, noxious can also describe plants. Noxious weeds are harmful plants that are a pest to farms, and landowners must control them by law. A dictionary helps when you are not sure which meaning is being used.
fact: Noxious means harmful or poisonous, or very unpleasant.
fact: Noxious gases can come from cars, factories and fires, and they can make people ill.
fact: Never mix cleaning products, because they can give off noxious fumes.
fact: «Noxious weeds» are harmful plants that are a pest to farms (used in Australia, the US and Canada).
fact: Noxious is an adjective, so you can say more noxious to compare two things.
exercise: «The smoke from the factory chimney was noxious, so the workers wore masks.» What does noxious mean here? | Very cheerful | *Harmful and poisonous | Fluffy and white | Loud and noisy
exercise: «The bin gave off a noxious smell that made Sam hold his nose.» What does noxious describe? | A bright light | A happy song | *A very unpleasant smell | A kind, warm breeze
exercise: Ella says, «Never mix cleaning products, they give off noxious fumes.» Why should you never mix them? | Because they smell of lemons | *Because the fumes can be harmful | Because they make the bottles shiny | Because they are always free
test: «The rotten eggs gave off a noxious stink.» What does noxious mean? | Warm and gentle | Bright and shiny | *Very unpleasant | Quiet and soft
test: In Australia, what are «noxious weeds»? | *Harmful plants that farmers must control | Pretty flowers for the garden | Weeds that make cakes taste better | Tall trees growing near rivers
exam: Which meaning fits best in «Noxious fumes filled the garage.»? | Sweet smelling | *Harmful or poisonous | Dark blue | Very tiny
